# Data Explorer

## Section

Changeset and query exploration for the Tracker domain. Attach to the
running app first (**Runtime settings → Attached node**,
`financial_tracking@web.internal` + `LIVEBOOK_COOKIE`). Read-only unless you opt
in — every cell here either builds changesets in memory or queries.

## Setup

```elixir
import Ecto.Query

alias FinancialTracking.Repo
alias FinancialTracking.Tracker
alias FinancialTracking.Tracker.{ExecutiveBudget, Office, Purchase}

# Same helper DataCase gives tests: changeset errors as a readable map.
errors_on = fn changeset ->
  Ecto.Changeset.traverse_errors(changeset, fn {message, opts} ->
    Regex.replace(~r"%{(\w+)}", message, fn _, key ->
      opts |> Keyword.get(String.to_existing_atom(key), key) |> to_string()
    end)
  end)
end
```

## Probe a changeset

Feed candidate attrs and inspect what validates, what casts, and what
gets ignored. Useful for designing a validation before writing its test.

```elixir
attrs = %{name: "Team lunch", amount: "125.75", is_tax: false}

changeset = Tracker.change_purchase(%Purchase{}, attrs)
{changeset.valid?, changeset.changes, errors_on.(changeset)}
```

```elixir
# Empty attrs → see every required-field error at once.
errors_on.(Tracker.change_budget_line_item(%ExecutiveBudget{}, %{}))
```

```elixir
# What survives the cast? Keys absent from `changes` were not cast —
# e.g. Purchase currently ignores :notes, :concur_expense_report, :event.
Purchase.changeset(%Purchase{}, %{name: "x", notes: "dropped?", event: 3}).changes
```

## Browse live data

```elixir
Repo.all(from o in Office, order_by: o.name, preload: [:children, :parent])
```

```elixir
Repo.all(
  from p in Purchase,
    order_by: [desc: p.purchased_at],
    limit: 20,
    preload: [:origin_office]
)
```

```elixir
# Allocated budget rolled up per office.
Repo.all(
  from eb in ExecutiveBudget,
    join: o in assoc(eb, :office),
    group_by: o.name,
    select: {o.name, sum(eb.allocated)}
)
```
